Alembic migrations.

The database URL is not stored in alembic.ini. env.py reads it from the application
settings, so the credential lives only in .env or in the deployment environment.

Create a revision after changing a model:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

Read what was generated before applying it. Autogenerate is good at columns and
constraints and blind to anything that needs data moved, so a renamed column arrives as a
drop followed by an add unless it is rewritten by hand.

Apply it, roll back one step, and confirm the models and the database still agree:

    alembic upgrade head
    alembic downgrade -1
    alembic check

Reference data is not loaded here. A migration that imports application code breaks as
soon as that code moves on, so the service catalogue is installed by
`fleetkeeper sync-catalog`, which is safe to re-run against any version.
